  "visual_observation": "At frame12 the far actor turquoise fill and cream rings remain visible through outlined gaps between veil-I leaves. Baseline retains that exposed artwork. Candidate1 fills part of those gaps with the stationary mural, cutting away the visible rings and fill. The source-backed witnesses lie3px or farther from true foreground, outside the disclosed2px allowance, and the same omission is exact in the preencode PNG. The near actor also loses exposed cream tail detail at the front veil in frame12.",
  "grader_alignment": "The visible-source-pattern rejection is supported by an actual local over-occlusion rather than solely a codec or canonical sampling difference. Passing true-foreground/depth checks is compatible with this defect: source foreground pixels keep their order while extra stationary background incorrectly covers the actor. This audit does not attempt to attribute every part of the numerical failure.",
